# Printed by pacman after install. The package deliberately does not edit
# ~/.xscreensaver: that file belongs to the user, xscreensaver rewrites it
# wholesale, and a package has no business owning a line in it. So the one
# manual step is explained here rather than done silently.

post_install() {
	cat <<'EOF'

gibson-screensaver is installed, but xscreensaver will not list it until you
add it to your own configuration. Add this line to the "programs:" list in
~/.xscreensaver (run xscreensaver-settings once first if that file does not
exist yet):

    gibson-screensaver

It takes no arguments; the daemon and the settings dialog each pass the window
they want it to draw into. It appears in the hack list as "Hack the Gibson".

This is an X11 hack. On Wayland there is no xscreensaver, so run it from your
idle daemon instead, for example:

    swayidle -w timeout 300 'gibson-screensaver --fullscreen'

It needs a working Vulkan driver. If it fails to start, install the driver for
your GPU (see this package's optdepends) and check with vulkaninfo.

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
	# Nothing to say on upgrade: the programs: line, if present, still works,
	# because neither the binary name nor its arguments have changed.
	:
}
